          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em graded algebra
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            which is with a labelling on its elements by elements of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            will be an abelian group, and often by default
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = \mathbb{N}
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              \-graded ring
            or simply a
            %strong graded ring
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            equipped with a decomposition of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \oplus_{m \in M} R_m
            such that the product maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi m
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{m} \times R_{m'}
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mi m
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{m m'}
          %p
            Analogously there is the notion of graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            over any field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              \-graded algebra
            or simply
            %strong graded algebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+category"} monoid in a monoidal category
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p Both graded rings and graded algebras over a field are, in turn, special cases of graded algebras over a commutative ring.
          %p
            An
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            = succeed "." do
              %strong nonnegatively graded ring
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            %em connected
            if in degree zero it is just the ground ring.
          %p
            A
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} differential graded algebra
            is a graded algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d : A\to A
            of degree +1 (or -1, depending on conventions) and such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \circ d = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          %p#StronglyGraded
            A
            = succeed "-graded" do
